  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "In a word $\\mathrm{COCHIN}$, the second place can be filled in ${ }^4 C_1$ ways and the remaining four alphabets can be arranged in $4 !$ ways in four different places. The next $97^{\\text {th }}$ word will be COCHIN.",
